{"type":"tool_result","callId":"call_c6bf85c9275f462a8997b83a","status":"completed","result":"src/adapters/dsh/cognition.ts:129:        actions: [\"profile\", \"recommend\", \"explain\"],\nsrc/adapters/dsh/cognition.ts:152:          return advisor.explain(input);\nsrc/adapters/dsh/common.ts:252:    summary: {\nsrc/adapters/dsh/continuity.ts:20:        \"Read the project's CURRENT UNDERSTANDING with its standing and basis, or the DECISION-ORIENTED PULSE for continuing the project. `pulse` is the first read for a new Session: it combines the current goal and binding constraints, accepted assets, candidates, negative findings, open questions, recent material changes, pending Work, recorded contributions and their decision chain, in-flight / terminal / interrupted delegations, and two deliberately separate next-action lists — `mechanical` (what the product can legally execute) and `decisionRelevant` (advisory judgements, never authority). `summary` separates accepted-for-purpose facts, delivered candidates, negative findings, open questions/interpretations, pending work and blocked effects; every item carries source refs, the project revision/head it was derived at, and what would reopen it. `explain` returns the same facts for one ref (e.g. journal:pje-…, task:…, commit:…, requirement:…). `context_capsule` renders the same projection under a hard byte budget; when a section does not fit it is named in `omitted` and `complete` is false — the capsule never silently drops a safety fact. This is a DERIVED read: it owns no store and cannot accept, approve, plan or promote anything.\",\nsrc/adapters/dsh/continuity.ts:22:      actions: [\"pulse\", \"summary\", \"explain\", \"context_capsule\"],\nsrc/adapters/dsh/continuity.ts:24:        subject: { type: \"string\", description: \"for explain: a projection id or source ref\" },\nsrc/adapters/dsh/continuity.ts:28:        if (action === \"pulse\") return workspace.pulse();\nsrc/adapters/dsh/continuity.ts:29:        if (action === \"summary\") return workspace.summary();\nsrc/adapters/dsh/continuity.ts:30:        if (action === \"explain\") return workspace.explain(requiredString(object, \"subject\"));\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:37:      \"The NORMAL project work path. DIRECT WORK IS A FIRST-CLASS PATH: a formal Task is not required for every edit, and a project may hold a direct Git outcome without inventing Work. If the work was already committed outside a governed attempt, do NOT create a task to reproduce it — record an episode conclusion (`conclude`); a zero-delta attempt cannot be `complete`d, and a redundant formal task is retired by removing it from the plan (`plan` with tasks:[]) once the project is quiescent, not by faking settlement or by mislabelling it as a typed invalidation. Use it for ordinary work on this project: read the state (`status`), revise the plan (`plan`), advance what the product can do mechanically (`next`, `run`), start a REAL worker in its own execution world (`delegate`), observe who is actually running (`workers`), request a stop without pretending it happened (`stop`), inspect a delivered result and choose a safe continuation route (`results`, `continue`), take the next claimable work position (`start`), open a new single governed position (`begin`), close it when done (`complete`), record the EPISODE-LEVEL conclusion when the current work episode should stop (`conclude`), save a follow-up proposal without forcing the current plan (`propose`), or record an exploratory finding (`explore` / `explorations`). `delegate` executes an EXISTING canonical task; it does not invent work, and the worker may only report; the product observes the world and settles. `workers` distinguishes canonical attempt state from host-local job observation: a RUNNING attempt with no job in this host is NOT proven alive. `stop` is a REQUEST. `results` reports the packaged continuation assessment for the latest COMPLETED result, including path-level reuse facts (unaffected / conflicted / already-present) that a NEW governed task may use without accepting the old result, and `continue` carries the inspection digest into rematerialization or governed rework; neither accepts or promotes anything. `relay` continues an attempt whose worker is no longer running: `takeover` keeps the SAME attempt and world after an observed worker exit (or your explicit `declareExecutorAbandoned` declaration) and records PRINCIPAL_RECOVERY; `successor` closes an attempt this host cannot prove quiescent, keeps its world, and returns path-level reuse facts so a NEW attempt continues the still-valid work in a new world at the same basis. Every settlement reports the execution window the product OBSERVED (`ORIGINAL_WORKER_OBSERVED` / `SUBSEQUENT_WORKER_OBSERVED` / `PRINCIPAL_RECOVERY` / `MULTI_EXECUTOR` / `UNATTRIBUTED`); your own writing is never reported as worker production, and a principal takeover is not independent verification. `conclude` records YOUR judgement about the episode (DELIVER / WAIT_FOR_OPERATOR / WAIT_FOR_EXTERNAL_EVENT / REPLAN / CONTINUE / CHECKPOINT) and the product checks it against real facts: open tasks, live attempts, pending operator acceptance, blocked effects, artifact existence and artifact Git provenance. A refused conclusion names the contradiction; a recorded one is still NOT acceptance or promotion. Provenance warnings (an artifact untracked or uncommitted) are reported in the result and in the pulse; they do not by themselves refuse DELIVER. `readiness` reports the CURRENT outcome facts from the owners (attempt/world/commit/uncommitted/current inputs/completion) and classifies the next step as CONTINUE_WORK, SEMANTIC_JUDGEMENT or MECHANICAL_FINALIZATION; it is a read, not a permission. When it returns MECHANICAL_FINALIZATION, `finalize` with its `observationDigest` performs the bounded mechanical chain (fresh observation, existing completion evaluation, canonical settlement, existing scheduler progress) and stops before operator acceptance; a stale digest is refused, and a candidate that still needs a semantic judgement is refused rather than settled. After a recorded conclusion with `session.mayEnd=true`, reply to the user and stop calling tools unless something contradicts it. `explore` is the EXPLORATORY path: research, comparison, source inspection and tentative analysis are recorded as findings with sources and uncertainty, and create NO Task, Attempt, Evidence, Promotion or ProjectIR change. Use `plan` only for a governed commitment; independent research should not be represented as several formal Work tasks whose first result blocks the others. It never accepts an attempt id, an exit code, an evidence predicate or an approval. Every status/begin/complete reply carries the ACTUAL execution boundary: in-place edits change the live repository immediately, while worktree edits are an isolated candidate until an authorized Promotion. A proposal is NON-AUTHORITATIVE.\",\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:70:      summary: { type: \"string\", description: \"for complete: what you consider done, in your own words\" },\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:80:      evidenceRefs: { type: \"array\", items: { type: \"string\" }, description: \"for conclude: journal/commit/result refs supporting the judgement; a negative DELIVER must cite a recorded negative finding\" },\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:267:        const summary = object.summary;\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:268:        if (summary !== undefined && typeof summary !== \"string\") throw new ToolArgsError('argument \"summary\" must be a string when given');\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:274:          ...(summary === undefined ? {} : { summary }),\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:289:        const summary = object.summary;\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:290:        if (summary !== undefined && typeof summary !== \"string\") throw new ToolArgsError('argument \"summary\" must be a string when given');\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:301:              ...(summary === undefined ? {} : { summary }),\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:344:              ...(summary === undefined ? {} : { summary }),\nsrc/adapters/dsh/normal.ts:376:        const result = await work.finish(summary === undefined ? {} : { summary });\nsrc/adapters/dsh/outcome.ts:21:        \"Read and evaluate the project's BUSINESS OUTCOME separately from Work de","truncated":true}
