{"type":"thinking","text":"Use same test helper.\n\nMaybe use archive itself in a test to prove actual old project. Could write test that loads `owners/journal.sqlite` and `palettes...` via copying to temp with repo from bundle. But maybe too slow. Yet user explicitly asks \"请用现有的归档项目复现\". We can add test using archive files directly with DatabaseSync plus reconstructed service? But we can more simply use archive DBs and the existing bundle through `git` command in test, then installProduct using profile. This is feasible and strong. Test can:\n- create temp\n- `git init world`, `git fetch bundle refs/heads/accepted`, checkout FETCH_HEAD\n- copy owners palimpsest.sqlite/journal.sqlite into state\n- installProduct {projectId:\"grpc-migration-continuation\", repository:world, stateDir:state, execution:\"in-place\", standard maybe need standard? installProduct works without standard maybe normal.}\n- call `palimpsest_continuity pulse`, summary, explain.\nBut archive owners includes only palimpsest/journal; installProduct creates ordarium maybe existing missing? It may create. Profiles in archive used expected state dirs with multiple DBs but those not saved; install may initialize? Could work. More reliable to use product after restore profile? The archive's `restore` script only copies palimpsest and journal, then profile has all DB paths; DSH host may initialize missing. Our installProduct stateDir only uses those two DBs plus ordarium created; should be okay.\n- Need standard? installProduct standard optional. If no standard, project loaded from DB already initialized. Might work.\n- Then assert actual IDs. This explicitly uses existing archive, satisfying user. But test should not depend on external file path? It's repo relative. Fine. Maybe copying DB from archive into temp and not modifying archive (read-only). Use `copyFileSync`. Need avoid huge bundle checkout? small.\n- Could add one archive regression test and one pure/new project scenario test. This also cov