` same, `revision:${currentRevision}` maybe.\n- note journal IDs? Could include verification note source refs for accepted version and deliver? We can compute matching note IDs and add `journal:<noteId>` to conclusion item sourceRefs if note commit matches delivered. That directly connects old conclusion -> verification note. Nice.\n\nLet's implement helper in service build:\n```\nconst conclusionEntries = entries.flatMap...\nconst recordedObservations = ...\nconst acceptedVersionCommit = status.directOutcome?.admittedDirectCommit ?? null;\nconst observationNoteIdsForCommit = (commit) => recordedObservations.filter(item => item.sourceRefs.includes(`commit:${commit}`)).map(item => item.id)\n```\nBut recordedObservations built as items; for conclusion build source refs can use entries raw.\n\nOrdering matters: compute episodeConclusions after recordedObservations? We can compute raw recorded entries helper functions, then build.\n\nSimpler:\n```\nconst episodeRecords = entries.map(view=> ({view, conclusion: parse...})).filter...\nconst observationViews = entries.filter(...)\nconst acceptedVersionCommit = ...\nconst noteIdsForCommit = (commit) => observationViews.filter(view => relatedCommitIds(view).includes(commit)).map(view=>`journal:${view.entry.entryId}`)\nconst episodeConclusions = episodeRecords.map(({view, conclusion}) => {\n const delivered = episodeDeliveredCommits(conclusion); // helper imported\n const refs = ...\n if (acceptedVersionCommit && delivered.some(matches)) refs.push(...noteIdsForCommit(acceptedVersionCommit))\n ...\n})\nconst recordedObservations = observationViews.map...\n```\nNeed helper `episodeDeliveredCommits` exported from episode.ts; can import. Also `commitRefsMatch` maybe export from episode. Or local in service. We can define exported helpers in episode.ts:\n```\nexport function conclusionDeliveredCommits(conclusion: EpisodeConclusion): readonly string[]\nexport function commitRefMatches(recorded: string, accepted: string): boolean\n``