{"type":"thinking","text":"Let's patch episode with helpers and accepted logic. Need careful existing tests. We'll modify changedSince collection to categorize.\n\nDefine helpers before buildPulseEpisode:\n```\nexport function episodeDeliveredCommits(conclusion: EpisodeConclusion): readonly string[] { ... }\nexport function commitReferenceMatches(recorded: string, accepted: string): boolean { ... }\n```\nMaybe names not conflict.\n\nAlgorithm:\n```\nconst deliveredCommits = episodeDeliveredCommits(conclusion);\nconst accepted = input.acceptedVersion;\nconst acceptedDelivery = accepted !== undefined && accepted !== null && accepted !== \"\" && deliveredCommits.some(c => commitReferenceMatches(c, accepted));\nconst basisChanged: string[] = ...\nconst journalChanges: string[] = ...\nconst artifactChanges = ...\nconst taskChanges = ...\nconst nonBasis = [...journalChanges,...artifactChanges,...taskChanges]\nconst changedSince = [...basisChanged,...nonBasis]\nconst current = changedSince.length === 0 || (acceptedDelivery && nonBasis.length===0)\nconst effectiveChanged = current ? [] : changedSince\nstate current ? INTENT... : REOPENED\ndetail:\n if current && acceptedDelivery: `the conclusion's recorded delivery ${deliveredCommits[0]} is the currently accepted project version; the judgement remains historical evidence...`\n else if current: existing\n else ...\nacceptedVersion: acceptedDelivery ? accepted : null? maybe undefined\ndeliveredVersion: deliveredCommits[0] ?? null\n```\nBut if basisChanged empty and changedSince empty with accepted delivery true, detail should still mention acceptance. We can condition `acceptedDelivery && current` first.\n\nFor no conclusion return add `deliveredVersion:null, acceptedVersion:null` optional fields maybe hidden not. Add always? Not necessary but consistent. We'll include.\n\nNeed avoid repeated `deliveredCommits` when acceptedVersion undefined. Fine.\n\nShould `current` true if acceptedDelivery and journalChanges nonempty but all journal changes are not basis relevant? They won't be in journalChanges. If plain note remains -> false. Good.\n\nShould artifactChanges from current artifact states be empty after acceptance. Good.\n\nPatch."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_59067eee0dd64c989d7fc765","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/project_continuity/episode.ts')\ns=p.read_text()\nold='''export interface PulseEpisode {\n  readonly state: EpisodeState;\n  readonly conclusion: EpisodeConclusion | null;\n  /** False when the project revised, moved its head, or recorded any journal fact after the conclusion. */\n  readonly current: boolean;\n  readonly changedSince: readonly string[];\n  readonly readiness: EpisodeReadiness;\n  readonly detail: string;\n}\n\nconst INTENT_STATE: Readonly<Record<EpisodeIntent, EpisodeState>> = Object.freeze({\n'''\nnew='''export interface PulseEpisode {\n  readonly state: EpisodeState;\n  readonly conclusion: EpisodeConclusion | null;\n  /** False when the project revised, moved its head, or recorded any journal fact after the conclusion. */\n  readonly current: boolean;\n  readonly changedSince: readonly string[];\n  readonly readiness: EpisodeReadiness;\n  readonly detail: string;\n  /**\n   * The version the conclusion itself named (the full commit from recorded artifact provenance, or\n   * the commit evidence when no artifact was observed). This is the DELIVERED version, not an\n   * acceptance claim.\n   */\n  readonly deliveredVersion?: string | null | undefined;\n  /**\n   * The currently accepted version, but ONLY when this conclusion's recorded delivery is that exact\n   * version. A later accepted version that does not contain this delivery is a genuine supersession,\n   * not a confirmation, and is left to `changedSince`/the current basis.\n   */\n  readonly acceptedVersion?: string | null | undefined;\n}\n\n/**\n * The exact commits a conclusion recorded for the bytes it delivered. Artifact provenance is the\n * strongest source (it names the full commit actually read); evidence refs are the fallback and may\n * be abbreviated. A short evidence commit is expanded only when a recorded artifact commit starts\n * with it, so no prefix is silently treated as a different version.\n */\nexport function episodeDeliveredCommits(conclusion: EpisodeConclusion): readonly string[] {\n  const commits = new Set<string>();\n  for (const artifact of conclusion.check.artifacts ?? []) {\n    if (typeof artifact.commit === \"string\" && artifact.commit !== \"\") commits.add(artifact.commit);\n  }\n  for (const ref of conclusion.evidenceRefs) {\n    if (!ref.startsWith(\"commit:\")) continue;\n    const value = ref.slice(\"commit:\".length).trim();\n    if (value === \"\") continue;\n    const full = [...commits].find((commit) => commit.startsWith(value));\n    commits.add(full ?? value);\n  }\n  return Object.freeze([...commits]);\n}\n\n/** Compare a recorded commit (possibly abbreviated) with an accepted full commit. */\nexport function commitReferenceMatches(recorded: string, accepted: string): boolean {\n  if (recorded === accepted) return true;\n  if (recorded.length < 7 || accepted.length < 7) return false;\n  return accepted.startsWith(recorded) || recorded.startsWith(accepted);\n}\n\nconst INTENT_STATE: Readonly<Record<EpisodeIntent, EpisodeState>> = Object.freeze({\n'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nold2='''  readonly basisRelevant?: ((entry: JournalFact) => boolean) | undefined;\n}): PulseEpisode {\n'''\nnew2='''  readonly basisRelevant?: ((entry: JournalFact) => boolean) | undefined;\n  /**\n   * The currently accepted canonical version, when the caller can observe it. When the conclusion's\n   * recorded delivery IS that version, the acceptance confirms the conclusion rather than reopening\n   * it: the old episode becomes historical evidence, not an open task.\n   */\n  readonly acceptedVersion?: string | null | undefined;\n}): PulseEpisode {\n'''\nassert old2 in s\ns=s.replace(old2,new2)\nold3='''  if (conclusion === null) {\n    return Object.freeze({\n      state: \"OPEN\",\n      conclusion: null,\n      current: true,\n      changedSince: Object.freeze([]),\n      readiness: input.readiness,\n      detail:\n        \"no episode conclusion is recorded; this episode is OPEN. Continue the work, or record a conclusion when the goal has been handled, acceptance is pending, an external fact is awaited, or a checkpoint is the honest next state\",\n    });\n  }\n\n  const changedSince: string[] = [];\n  if (conclusion.basis.projectRevision !== input.basis.projectRevision) {\n    changedSince.push(`project revision moved from ${String(conclusion.basis.projectRevision)} to ${String(input.basis.projectRevision)}`);\n  }\n  if (conclusion.basis.headCommit !== input.basis.headCommit) {\n    changedSince.push(`repository head moved from ${conclusion.basis.headCommit.slice(0, 12)} to ${input.basis.headCommit.slice(0, 12)}`);\n  }\n  const relevant = input.basisRelevant;\n  for (const entry of input.entries.slice(lastIndex + 1)) {\n    if (relevant !== undefined && !relevant(entry)) continue;\n    changedSince.push(`journal ${entry.entryId} (${entry.kind}) \"${entry.title}\" was recorded after the conclusion`);\n  }\n  /**\n   * PWRS-C artifact currentness. Compared only when BOTH sides carry a digest: an old conclusion\n   * (recorded before digests existed) cannot be reopened by a fact it never recorded, and pretending\n   * otherwise would manufacture a change.\n   */\n  if (input.artifactStatesNow !== undefined) {\n    changedSince.push(...artifactChangeReasons(conclusion.check.artifacts ?? [], input.artifactStatesNow));\n  }\n  /** A pending operator acceptance that was resolved is a real change, not a stale judgement. */\n  if (input.taskStates !== undefined) {\n    for (const ref of conclusion.check.awaitingOperator) {\n      const taskId = ref.startsWith(\"task:\") ? ref.slice(\"task:\".length) : ref;\n      const state = input.taskStates.get(taskId);\n      if (state === \"SATISFIED\") {\n        changedSince.push(`the operator accepted task ${taskId}; the pending acceptance the conclusion named is resolved`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  const current = changedSince.length === 0;\n\n  return Object.freeze({\n    state: current ? INTENT_STATE[conclusion.intent] : \"REOPENED\",\n    conclusion,\n    current,\n    changedSince: Object.freeze(changedSince),\n    readiness: input.readiness,\n    detail: current\n      ? `the principal recorded ${conclusion.intent} at revision ${String(conclusion.basis.projectRevision)}; this is a judgement, not acceptance, and the operator retains authority`\n      : `the conclusion is REOPENED: ${changedSince.join(\"; \")}. Re-read the current state before relying on the earlier judgement`,\n  });\n}\n'''\nnew3='''  const deliveredCommits = episodeDeliveredCommits(conclusion);\n  const acceptedVersion = input.acceptedVersion ?? null;\n  /**\n   * A later acceptance that lands exactly on the recorded delivery confirms the judgement. The basis\n   * moved, but not in a way that contradicts the delivered bytes. Any OTHER later fact still counts:\n   * only basis movement is ignored, and only for this exact match. Weaker evidence is never enough to\n   * claim acceptance (a different or later accepted version stays a real supersession).\n   */\n  const acceptedDelivery =\n    acceptedVersion !== null &&\n    acceptedVersion !== \"\" &&\n    deliveredCommits.some((commit) => commitReferenceMatches(commit, acceptedVersion));\n\n  if (conclusion === null) {\n    return Object.freeze({\n      state: \"OPEN\",\n      conclusion: null,\n      current: true,\n      changedSince: Object.freeze([]),\n      readiness: input.readiness,\n      deliveredVersion: null,\n      acceptedVersion: null,\n      detail:\n        \"no episode conclusion is recorded; this episode is OPEN. Continue the work, or record a conclusion when the goal has been handled, acceptance is pending, an external fact is awaited, or a checkpoint is the honest next state\",\n    });\n  }\n\n  const basisChanges: string[] = [];\n  if (conclusion.basis.projectRevision !== input.basis.projectRevision) {\n    